## Re-census (freshness guard)

Counts go stale as the code evolves. Before relying on a row, re-verify cheaply:

```bash
# per symbol (run from the project root):
grep -rl '<Symbol>' . --exclude-dir=node_modules --exclude-dir=.git \
  --exclude-dir=coverage --exclude-dir=reports --exclude-dir=dist --exclude-dir=.next | wc -l
# (prefer `rg -l '<Symbol>' | wc -l` when ripgrep is available — it respects .gitignore,
#  so local test/build artifacts never inflate the count)
```

If the count diverges from this file, the map is stale: re-run the generator
(full, or delta: `scan_project.py <root> --update <changed-paths>`) before trusting it.

## Rules

1. **Modify a listed surface ⇒ check its consumers first.** Keep the contract
   (signature, props, behavior, emitted events) or bring every consumer's adaptation
